  +# Self-Update Summary
  +
  +## Original Requirements
  +The original requirements are outlined in the `README.md` of the self-update plan. They include:
  +- **Explicit commands**: `cpe update` to install the latest version and `cpe update --check` to verify the current vs latest version.
  +- **Automatic updating**: Background auto-update every 6 hours when running `cpe start`, and a nudge every 24 hours for short-lived CLI commands.
  +- **Configuration**: `update_auto?: boolean` in `~/.config/cpe/config.json`, default `true`. Dev builds (`CPE_VERSION === 'dev'`) are exempt.
  +- **Release integrity**: Each GitHub release now includes a `SHA256SUMS` file for binary verification.
  +- **Technical approach**: Use a redirect to `https://github.com/richardbenson/claude-plan-executor/releases/latest` to resolve the latest tag, and perform an atomic swap of the binary with verification.
  +
  +## What Was Built
  +The implementation followed the four phases:
  +
  +### Phase 01 – Release checksums
  +- Added `SHA256SUMS` generation to the GitHub release workflow (`release.yml`).
  +- Updated `scripts/install.sh` to download and verify the checksum when present.
  +
  +### Phase 02 – Updater core module
  +- Implemented `src/update/check.ts`, `src/update/install.ts`, and `src/update/state.ts` to resolve the latest tag, compare versions, download/install with verification, and manage check-state.
  +
  +### Phase 03 – CLI surface
  +- Added `cpe update` and `cpe update --check` commands in `src/commands/update.ts`.
  +- Introduced `update_auto` flag in `AppConfig` and wired the nudge logic in `src/update/nudge.ts`.
  +- Updated `README.md` to document the new commands and configuration.
  +
  +### Phase 04 – TUI auto-update loop & footer badge
  +- Implemented `src/update/auto.ts` with a background loop checking every 6 hours and installing newer releases.
  +- Added a persistent yellow footer badge in `src/tui/Watch.tsx`, `src/tui/Manage.tsx`, and `src/tui/Bench.tsx` to indicate an update is installed but requires restart.
  +- Updated `docs/DESIGN.md` to specify badge placement, color (`#e0af68`), and behavior.
  +
  +The git log (`git log --oneline feature/self-update`) confirms the commits for each phase were made on the `feature/self-update` branch, culminating in a merge to `main`.
  +
  +## Lessons Learned
  +- **Checksum integration** was straightforward once the release workflow was extended, but required careful handling of missing `SHA256SUMS` for older releases.
  +- **Atomic binary swap** using a temp file and `rename()` worked reliably across Linux and macOS, avoiding `ETXTBSY` errors.
  +- **Config flag** (`update_auto`) provided a clean opt-out mechanism without breaking existing configs.
  +- **TUI badge persistence** required a module‑scope store and a hook to keep the badge visible across renders and interactive subprocesses.
  +- **Testing** across phases ensured each component (version check, install, nudge, loop) behaved correctly, both with and without network access.
  +
  +Overall, the self‑update feature was successfully implemented, verified against the plan, and ready for release.
